      "suggested_text": "At that time Raphael, one of the holy angels who was with me, answered and said to me, “These hollow places[a] are for the spirits of the souls of the dead[b] to be gathered into them. For this purpose they were created here: to gather all the souls of the children of men.”",
      "footnote_changes": "Replace all notes. a, after 'hollow places': 'Charles marks the Ethiopic description as corrupt; note 22 identifies the same beautiful/hollow confusion discussed in verse 2.' b, after 'dead': 'Literally, “spirits of the souls of the dead.” This expression alone does not establish separate classes of spirits and souls.' Remove the unqualified 'good/beautiful places' alternatives and the unsupported claim that apposition is probably intended.",
      "suggested_source_text": "ውእቱ፡ ጊዜ፡ አውሥአ፡ ሩፋኤል፡ ፩*እምነ፡ ቅዱሳን፡ መላእክት፡ እንዘ፡ ሀለወ፡ ምስሌየ፡ ወይቤለኒ፡ ዝመካናት፡ †ሰናያት፡† ከመ፡ ይትጋብኡ፡ ዲቤሆን፡ *መናፍስት፡ ለነፍሶሙ፡ ለምዉታን፤ *ሎቱ፡ ዝንቱ፡ ተፈጥሩ፡ ዝየ፡ ያስተጋብኡ፡ ኵሎ፡ ነፍሰ፡ ውሉደ፡ ሰብእ።"
